*(stock-right
  <div id='datacenter_right_col'>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
      <span style="font-family: Verdana,Arial,sans-serif; font-size: 110%; margin-bottom: 6px;">
        <b>Stocks at MaizeGDB</b>
      </span>
      <br />
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
      <span style="font-family: Verdana, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 120%; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px;">Discussion of
      Stock Data for the General Public</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <u>
        <b>What is a stock?</b>
      </u>
    </p>
    <p>A 
    <b>stock</b> is a sample of corn that expresses a specific 
    <a href="variation">variation</a> (or a specific small set of variations\). Thus, stocks are living examples of variation
    data.</p>
    <br>
    <p>
      <u>
        <b>Why store stock data?</b>
      </u>
    </p>
    <p>Storing stock data makes it easy for scientists interested in a particular 
    <a href="variation">variation</a> or 
    <a href="locus">locus</a> to find and acquire living tissue that contains this desired 
    <a href="/data_center/variation">variation</a>.
    </p>
    <br />
    
  </div>
  )